Post-operative changes from aortic dissection repair are noted, with stent shadows visible along the arterial wall and a dense metallic shadow on the left side. There is decreased transparency in the left lung field, with patchy high-density opacities observed. The left hemidiaphragm appears blurred, and the left costophrenic angle is obscured, while the right hemidiaphragm and right costophrenic angle remain clear. There is distortion of the bony structure of the right 8th posterior rib. A left-sided central venous catheter is positioned at the level of the upper border of the T3 vertebral body. The tip of the endotracheal tube is located at the level of the T2 vertebral body.

In the abdomen, there are scattered gas shadows in the small and large intestines, with a significant amount of bowel contents present. No free air is seen under the diaphragm on either side, and there are no visible positive stones or calcifications. The tip of the nasogastric tube is positioned at the level of the upper border of the L3 vertebral body. Stent shadows are visible in the regions of the iliac vessels on both sides.

